xt": "disease:"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1669"}}, {"id": "body-05542", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Most of anti-TB medicines can cause liver damage. In case a patient develops jaundice, treatment should be stopped and restarted as soon as the jaundice resolves. In severely ill patients, start moxifloxacin and ethambutol only.", "runs": [{"text": "Most of anti-TB medicines can cause liver damage. In case a patient develops jaundice, treatment should be stopped and restarted as soon as the jaundice resolves. In severely ill patients, start moxifloxacin and ethambutol only."}]}, {"id": "body-05544", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Renal failure:", "runs": [{"text": "Renal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "failure:"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1669"}}, {"id": "body-05545", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The recommended initial treatment regimen for patients with renal failure or severe renal insufficiency is 2RHZE/4RH. Ethambutol and pyrazinamide should be used three times per week post dialysis according to the recommended dosage", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "initial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "regimen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "renal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "failure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "renal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "insufficiency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2RHZE/4RH. Ethambutol and pyrazinamide should be used three times per week post dialysis according to the recommended dosage"}]}, {"id": "body-05546", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "For transplant patients, rifampicin should be replaced by rifabutin as it has less interaction with im